# greenfield-proof

Private, unlicensed TypeScript greeting library and CLI for developers. Supports Node 22+ on Linux; use npm. No publishing, deployment, remotes, services or authentication.

```typescript
import { greet } from 'greenfield-proof';

greet(); // Hello, world!
greet('Ada'); // Hello, Ada!
```

Build before importing the package or running the CLI. Blank names are rejected; [UX canon](docs/ux-canon.md) defines help, errors and exit codes.

## Structure

| Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| package.json, package-lock.json | Private package metadata, scripts and npm resolution |
| src/index.ts | Typed greeting API |
| src/cli.ts | Executable process adapter |
| tsup.config.ts | ESM and declaration build |
| tsconfig.json, tsconfig.test.json | Compiler and built-import checks |
| test/greeting.test.mjs, test/cli.test.mjs | Meaningful behavior tests |
| test/types/greeting.ts | Public declaration contract check |
| dist/ | Generated JavaScript and declarations |
| docs/PRD.md | Requirements, fixture decisions and approval |
| docs/adr/ | Stack and design decisions |
| docs/architecture.md | Canonical architecture index |
| docs/ux-canon.md | Terminal interaction contract |
| docs/CODE-STYLE.md | Actual compiler, lint and format policy |
| AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md | Conventions and harness pointer |
| scripts/check-readme-catalog.mjs | README catalog guard |
| roadmap/roadmap.config.json | Gate and design-home bindings |
| roadmap/lib/ | Scaffolded schema, registry and emitter |
| roadmap/ROADMAP.md, roadmap/backlog.ts | Workflow home and empty execution queue |
| roadmap/phases/, roadmap/arcs/ | Empty planning homes |
| scripts/pre-review.sh, scripts/collect-phase-metrics.ts | Scaffolded review helpers |
| scripts/build-dashboard.sh, scripts/generate-changelog-md.ts | Scaffolded presentation helpers |
| reviews/releases/ | Empty release-review home |
| reviews/changelog.json | Generated roadmap emission |
| .gitignore | Generated-output and local-state exclusions |
| .npm-cache/, .npm-logs/ | Ignored scratch-local npm state |

## Commands

Run from the repository root. Keep npm state inside scratch in each shell:

```sh
export npm_config_cache="$PWD/.npm-cache"
export npm_config_logs_dir="$PWD/.npm-logs"
```

| Command | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| npm ci | Install locked dependencies; uses network when cache misses |
| npm run build | Build API, CLI and declarations before subsequent checks |
| npm run type-check | Check source and typed public import |
| node --test | Run API and CLI behavior tests |
| npm test | Alias for node --test |
| node dist/cli.js Ada | Print Hello, Ada! |
| node dist/cli.js --help | Built CLI integration smoke check |
| npm run emit:phases | Emit the roadmap changelog |
| npm run changelog:md | Scaffolded changelog helper; not required by initialization |
| node scripts/check-readme-catalog.mjs --project-root . | Validate this catalog |
| node /home/patrik/zeroh-marketplace-codex-29-30-31-32-33-34/plugins/zeroh-roadmap/bin/roadmap.mjs config check | Validate roadmap bindings using the local plugin |

Lint and browser e2e gates are explicitly absent, not passing tests. No formatter is installed. Build, types, unit, integration and emit are required. Scaffolded auxiliary helpers are retained but are not initialization gates or authorization to perform release work.

## Catalog

<!-- repo-catalog:start -->
| Project | Path | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| greenfield-proof | . | Typed greeting API and CLI fixture |
<!-- repo-catalog:end -->

